  200: *** THE LATCH-KEYED ACCEPT SHRINK (the K-CLASS) AND ITS CLOSURE -- repair 13, and it is the reason this probe grew
  201: from 157 rows to 188. ***
  202: 
  203: An accept guard grown with a conjunct on THIS FIX'S OWN LATCH -- `&& !(<cell> && (d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN))' -- declines
  204: SILENTLY at that cell once any refusal has happened, because the latch is exactly what suppresses the announce.  Three
  205: instances were MEASURED at 157/157 with a guest loss on the 157-row instrument (closing pass 7, opus_close7_20260915/
  206: OPUS_REPORT.md): K1 at INTMASK 4W, K2 at the REV 4-byte cell, K3 at CONTROL 8R.  The value rows at THOSE THREE
  207: CELLS are measured with the latch CLEAR, so none of them could see it.
  208: *** THIS SENTENCE READ "EVERY value row this probe had was measured with the latch CLEAR" AND IS FALSE -- codex,
  209: closing pass 8, naming `imask keeps', `sb keeps', `sh keeps' and the TIME controls as rows that already operate
  210: AFTER a refusal.  IT IS THE SECOND TIME I HAVE WRITTEN IT: the close-7 seat corrected the same over-generalisation
  211: in MAINLOOP_HARVEST.md (45 sessions, 72 post-refusal accepted accesses in eleven of them), and I reintroduced it
  212: here while writing repair 13's contract.  The true statement is the narrow one above, plus the derived bucket: of
  213: the 31 guest-visible ACCEPTS entries, EIGHT are already pinned post-latch (session_map2.py).  A sentence corrected
  214: once and rewritten later is worse than one never corrected, because the correction is on record and looks applied. ***
  215: 
  216: *** THE GRADE IS FLOOR, NOT CLAUSE (e), and that OVERTURNED THE PRIOR RULING (FABLE_C5_RULING_20260915.md, S-A.7;
  217: FABLE_C4_RULING's RA3 corrected in place).  The reason is in the fix's own diff: the width dispatch's `else' arm READS
  218: `d->warned', in a hunk this diff ADDS -- so the latch is a device-state lvalue the fix's own repair path reads, which
  219: the pass-11 floor definition and the M_ICLR precedent make a floor axis. ***
