  224: seat, closing pass 8, and it is the sharpest finding of that pass.  (i) THE LATCH-CLEAR HALF IS 28 CELLS AND TWELVE IS
  225: TWELVE.  (ii) Materially, and by this round's OWN evidence: close-7's E2 proved TIME 4W/4R guest-visible on a
  226: LATCH-CLEAR observation ("free-running ld;sw;ld reads 0xc6 then 0x108 on base and 0x0 under the bypass" -- no refusal
  227: in that sequence), and TIME 4W/4R are NOT among the twelve, whose only TIME cell is 8W.  So the half provably contains
  228: a guest-visible cell outside the set that was said to close it. ***
  229: *** AND THE CONSEQUENCE IS A CANDIDATE ESCAPE, THE MIRROR OF THE K-CLASS: repair 13 rows TIME 4W/4R ONLY POST-LATCH --
  230: every `p *' session opens with a refused lb, which is the whole point of them -- so a bypass conditioned on the latch
  231: being CLEAR has NO row running in its state at that cell.  The amended catching clause above ("CAUGHT ... AND THE
  232: CATCHING ROW RUNS IN THE BYPASS'S OWN LATCH STATE") therefore fails for it by its own words.  The owed row is the same
