| Historical bucket | Complete membership | Previously unnamed members |
|---|---|---|
| 10 EQUIVALENT | **1, 3, 4, 8, 12, 13, 16, 17, 43, 44** | **12, 13, 16, 17, 43, 44**: CONTROL writes of `0`, `0x0200`, and `0x0100`, each at both widths. |
| 5 host-observable, guest-equivalent | **10, 11, 14, 15, 40** | **11 and 15**: CONTROL `0x0001`, at four and eight bytes. |

The second row describes **observability**, not five remaining coverage debts. Four members are now ROWED, leaving only #40 in the exclusive HOST-DIAGNOSTIC ONLY disposition.

The historical eight incidental SET pins are **21, 23, 25, 27, 31, 34, 35, 46**. Their channels are respectively `istat ctl`, `imask keeps`, `imask ctl`, the DOG `keeps` rows, TIME controls, `lo keeps` for both its store and read, and the far-slot readbacks. The other 27 ROWED entries form the revised first bucket.

Two qualifications follow from reading the executable assertions:

- **#21 already has a SET effect oracle:** the accepted `lw` at P:843 raises IP2, checked by `istat ctl` at P:857. The “oracle-less” description at P:1534–1539 is too broad. Repair 14’s high-word **value** oracle is a separate strengthening.
